      "text": "Showing 1 to 20 of 48 entries\n1\n2\n3\nPortal Term\n\t\nDefinition\n\t\nOther Names\n\n\n\t\n\t\nCeiling Amount\n\t\nThe maximum amount the government can spend through a contract vehicle before it must be modified or replaced.\n\t\nContract ceiling, maximum value, spending limit, ceiling value\n\n\n8(a) Set-Aside\n\t\nAn opportunity reserved for businesses in the SBA 8(a) Business Development Program.\n\t\n8(a), SBA 8(a)\n\n\nPSC\n\t\nProduct and Service Code (PSC) - A code that describes the specific product or service the government is purchasing, such as software or medical supplies.\n\t\nProduct code, service code, federal supply code, PSC code\n\n\nAwarding Agency\n\t\nThe government organization responsible for issuing the award or contract.\n\t\nAwarding office, contracting office, issuing office, contracting agency\n\n\nSolicitation Number\n\t\nThe tracking number used to identify a government opportunity and its documents.\n\t\nSolicitation #, notice ID, opportunity number, solicitation ID\n\n\nStart Date\n\t\nThe day work is allowed to begin. Note: This may be different from the Date Signed.\n\t\nEffective date, active date, period start\n\n\nLocation\n\t\nThe listed city, state, or address where an agency or office is based.\n\t\nHeadquarters, office location, address\n\n\nBusiness Type Code\n\t\nA category used to classify your business for government tracking, such as Small Business, Women-Owned (WOSB), or Veteran-Owned (SDVOSB).\n\t\nBusiness type, business category, socioeconomic category, vendor type\n\n\nSDVOSB Set-Aside\n\t\nAn opportunity reserved for Service-Disabled Veteran-Owned Small Businesses.\n\t\nSDVOSB\n\n\nAcronym\n\t\nA shortened name used instead of a longer official name, such as DoD for Department of Defense.\n\t\nAbbreviation, short name\n\n\nRFX\n\t\nRequest for X (RFX) - A general term for government requests, including Requests for Information, Quotes, Proposals, and Bids.\n\t\nProcurement request, solicitation, sourcing request\n\n\nGSA eBUY\n\t\nGeneral Services Administration eBuy - An online system where agencies request quotes from approved GSA contract holders.\n\t\neBuy, GSA eBuy Portal\n\n\nSolicitation Type\n\t\nThe type of notice, such as Sources Sought, Request for Quote (RFQ), Request for Proposal (RFP), or Award Notice.\n\t\nNotice type, opportunity type, procurement type, notice category\n\n\nSole Source\n\t\nA contract awarded directly to one eligible business without full competition when allowed by law.\n\t\nSole-source award\n\n\nPartial Set-Aside\n\t\nAn opportunity where only part of the work is reserved for qualifying small businesses.\n\t\nPartial SB Set-Aside\n\n\nVOSB Set-Aside\n\t\nAn opportunity reserved for Veteran-Owned Small Businesses where applicable.\n\t\nVeteran-Owned Small Business\n\n\nContract Acronym\n\t\nA shortened version of a contract or vehicle name, such as GSA MAS.\n\t\nContract abbreviation, vehicle acronym, short title\n\n\nVehicle\n\t\nA pre-approved buying program the government uses to purchase goods or services more quickly.\n\t\nContract vehicle, acquisition vehicle, purchasing vehicle, ordering vehicle\n\n\nSmall Business Set-Aside\n\t\nAn opportunity that only qualifying small businesses can compete for.\n\t\nSB Set-Aside, Small Business\n\n\nTotal Small Business Set-Aside\n\t\nAn opportunity where only qualifying small businesses may submit offers.\n\t\nTotal SB Set-Aside\nShow: \n20\n40\n60\n80\n100\n Entries\nJump To:\nGo\n1\n2\n3",
